From 9508003e7adf15900e9a55b05b6686515afbea8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nekreshen@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:58:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] codegen: inline GPR/LR helpers, classify by function
 base, shared-tail entries, aliased vector packs

From ReStreet (FIFA Street 2012, the same EA engine family):
- __savegprlr_N/__restgprlr_N calls become always_inline copies (gprlr_inline.h).
- Branch targets are classified against the owning function's base, not the
  instruction address (a shared tail can overlap another node's blocks).
- An external branch into the middle of another function gets its own entry
  (shared tail, registers shared).
- A conditional branch out of a function calls the target and returns,
  instead of returning silently.
- Jump tables may dispatch to separately registered case functions.
- vpkuhus/vpkuwus and the vupk*/vpk* family preserve aliased sources.
